Consider the following Spring bean class and XML configuration:

public class Employee {
    public Employee(String name) {
        if (name == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("name cannot be null");
        }
    }
}

<bean id="employee" class="Employee">
    <constructor-arg value="#{null}"/>
</bean>

When the Spring ApplicationContext attempts to instantiate the 'employee' bean, what exception is thrown?

